          "An honest not-yet-verified note is better than a confident summary built on an unchecked field. The analyst owns the preparation standard; the owner owns the judgment call. Scope creep in client escalation usually starts with one small favour that nobody entryed. The handoff is complete when both sides know which decisions did not travel with the work. For this step, the written action is to record the client statement, the impact, and the owner.",
